; Colour-code protection: two attempts, then reset
;
; Reached by the RET at the end of #R$8400, never called. Clears the bitmap and
; the attributes to zero (black on black), then calls #R$86C3 with the prompt
; "Enter Code at grid location" (#R$858B). If the code was right (Z set) the game
; goes on at #R$87CA. Otherwise #R$86C3 is called again with "Sorry, try code at
; location" (#R$85AB); it shows a different grid cell, because #R$86C3 adds to
; FRAMES every time. A second wrong code jumps to $0000, which restarts the
; machine through the ROM. Checked in the simulator with wrong codes: the
; second prompt appears and the second miss reaches PC=$0000.
; .
; Hardware: writes the whole screen (bitmap and attributes); JP 0 resets the machine.
@label=RunCodeCheck
c$869F LD HL,$4000   ;
@isub=LD DE,SCREEN+1
 $86A2 LD DE,$4001   ;
@isub=LD BC,SCREEN_AND_ATTRS_SIZE-1
 $86A5 LD BC,$1AFF   ;
 $86A8 LD (HL),$00   ;
 $86AA LDIR          ;
 $86AC LD IX,$858B   ; first attempt message
 $86B0 CALL $86C3    ;
 $86B3 JP Z,$87CA    ; code correct: continue with the game
 $86B6 LD IX,$85AB   ; second attempt message
 $86BA CALL $86C3    ;
 $86BD JP Z,$87CA    ;
 $86C0 JP $0000      ; wrong twice: reset
